[2026-03-21T09:28:36Z] [USER] I get the error: fatal: Could not read from remote repository.

Please make sure you have the correct access rights
 how do I add permissions to my git?
[2026-03-21T09:28:46Z] [CLAUDE] You need to set up SSH key authentication on the RunPod instance. Two options:

**Option 1: Generate a new SSH key on RunPod and add it to GitHub**

```bash
# On RunPod
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "runpod"
cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
```

Copy the output and add it to GitHub: **Settings → SSH and GPG keys → New SSH key**

**Option 2: Copy your existing key from your local machine to RunPod**

```bash
# From your local machine
scp ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 root@<runpod-ip>:~/.ssh/id_ed25519
scp ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub root@<runpod-ip>:~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
ssh root@<runpod-ip> "chmod 600 ~/.ssh/id_ed25519"
```

After either option, test with:
```bash
ssh -T git@github.com
```

You should see "Hi youruser! You've successfully authenticated."

**Option 1 is safer** — it gives RunPod its own key you can revoke independently. If the spot instance is reclaimed, the key is gone but the persistent volume data stays. You can also use a GitHub **deploy key** (read-only) if you only need to pull, not push.
