[2026-03-21T15:06:14Z] [USER] There is no sudo on RunPod
[2026-03-21T15:06:27Z] [CLAUDE] On RunPod you should already be root. Check:

```bash
whoami
```

If you are root, the issue is that RunPod pods often run in a restricted container environment where you can't run Docker-in-Docker with regular `dockerd`. 

Instead of trying to run Docker on RunPod, let's run the Celery worker **directly** on the pod without Docker:

```bash
# Install Python deps (with GPU extras)
pip install uv
cd /workspace/gorm.ai
uv sync --extra ml --extra autogluon --extra chronos

# Set up the SSH tunnel
PROD_HOST=gorm.predictioninstitute.com PROD_USER=rune PROD_SSH_PORT=22 bash -c '
ssh -f -N \
    -L 5432:localhost:5433 \
    -L 6379:localhost:6380 \
    -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new \
    -o ServerAliveInterval=30 \
    rune@gorm.predictioninstitute.com
'

# Export env vars pointing to the tunneled services
export DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://gorm:gorm@localhost:5432/gorm_ai
export CELERY_BROKER_URL=redis://localhost:6379/1
export CELERY_RESULT_BACKEND=redis://localhost:6379/2
export REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0

# Start the Celery worker
cd /workspace/gorm.ai
python -m gorm_ai.tasks.worker_entrypoint
```
