[2026-03-21T15:41:54Z] [CLAUDE] Almost — you also need the SSH tunnel and env vars. Here's the full sequence:

```bash
# 1. SSH tunnel to Cassandra
ssh -f -N \
    -L 5432:localhost:5433 \
    -L 6379:localhost:6380 \
    -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new \
    -o ServerAliveInterval=30 \
    rune@gorm.predictioninstitute.com

# 2. Env vars
export DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://gorm:gorm@localhost:5432/gorm_ai
export CELERY_BROKER_URL=redis://localhost:6379/1
export CELERY_RESULT_BACKEND=redis://localhost:6379/2
export REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0

# 3. Pull latest code and start worker
cd /workspace/gormai
git pull
pip install -e ".[ml]"
PYTHONPATH=src python -m gorm_ai.tasks.worker_entrypoint
```

You might want to save that as a script on the persistent volume so you don't have to remember it each time:

```bash
cat > /workspace/start-worker.sh << 'EOF'
#!/bin/bash
set -euo pipefail

ssh -f -N \
    -L 5432:localhost:5433 \
    -L 6379:localhost:6380 \
    -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new \
    -o ServerAliveInterval=30 \
    rune@gorm.predictioninstitute.com

export DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://gorm:gorm@localhost:5432/gorm_ai
export CELERY_BROKER_URL=redis://localhost:6379/1
export CELERY_RESULT_BACKEND=redis://localhost:6379/2
export REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0

cd /workspace/gormai
git pull
pip install -e ".[ml]"
PYTHONPATH=src python -m gorm_ai.tasks.worker_entrypoint
EOF
chmod +x /workspace/start-worker.sh
```

Then next time just: `bash /workspace/start-worker.sh`
