[2026-03-22T05:37:46Z] [CLAUDE] You don't — RunPod pods run **inside** Docker, so you can't run Docker inside them (no nested Docker).

Instead, skip Docker and run the worker **directly** on the RunPod pod:

```bash
cd /workspace/gorm.ai
git pull

# Install dependencies with uv (should already be available)
uv sync --frozen --no-dev --extra ml --extra autogluon --extra chronos

# Set up SSH tunnel to your production DB/Redis
export PROD_HOST=your-server.example.com
export PROD_USER=your-ssh-user
bash scripts/runpod-deploy-direct.sh   # or manually:

# Start the Celery worker directly
export DATABASE_URL="postgresql+asyncpg://gorm:gorm@localhost:5432/gorm_ai"
export CELERY_BROKER_URL="redis://localhost:6379/0"
export CELERY_RESULT_BACKEND="redis://localhost:6379/0"
export PYTHONPATH="/workspace/gorm.ai/src"
export HF_HUB_CACHE="/workspace/models"

celery -A gorm_ai.tasks.celery_app worker --loglevel=info --pool=solo -Q gpu
```

