[2026-03-22T06:01:18Z] [CLAUDE] Here are all the available parameters for the fine-tuning script (`scripts/finetune_timesfm.py`):

**Data selection:**
| Parameter | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `--customer-ids` | all | Comma-separated customer UUIDs |
| `--outlet-group-ids` | none | Comma-separated outlet group UUIDs |
| `--outlet-ids` | all | Comma-separated outlet UUIDs |
| `--start-date` | all history | Sales on or after this date (YYYY-MM-DD) |
| `--end-date` | today | Sales on or before this date (YYYY-MM-DD) |

**Training hyperparameters:**
| Parameter | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `--context-length` | 512 | Context window fed to the model per step |
| `--horizon` | 7 | Forecast horizon used as training target |
| `--epochs` | 3 | Training epochs per outlet |
| `--lr` | 1e-5 | Learning rate (kept small to preserve pre-trained knowledge) |
| `--batch-size` | 32 | Training batch size |

**Model/output:**
| Parameter | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `--output` | `models/timesfm_finetuned` | Checkpoint output directory |
| `--base-checkpoint` | `google/timesfm-2.5-200m-pytorch` | Base model (only used when no local checkpoint exists) |
| `--force` | false | Re-process outlets already marked as done |

The script is resumable — it tracks per-outlet progress in the `finetune_progress` DB table and skips already-completed outlets on restart.
