[2026-03-23T09:02:54Z] [CLAUDE] ~883MB per checkpoint. That's the full model weights — every save is the same size since it's a complete snapshot, not a delta.

Copying 883MB after every outlet over a decent connection (say 50-100 Mbps) would take ~1-2 minutes. Depending on how many outlets you're processing and how long each takes to train, that's probably fine — it's your safety net against losing work if the pod dies.

Two options:

**A) rsync after every outlet** — safest, ~1-2 min overhead per outlet
**B) rsync every N outlets** (e.g. every 5) — less overhead, but you could lose up to N outlets of work

