[2026-03-23T12:27:28Z] [USER] How can I make sure docker compose ps redis is running when I start the application?
[2026-03-23T12:27:40Z] [CLAUDE] Redis has `restart: unless-stopped` so it should auto-start after a Docker restart. If it's currently down, it was likely stopped manually or Docker was restarted.

On your production server, just run:

```bash
docker compose up -d redis
```

This will start only Redis if it's stopped, and do nothing if it's already running. It's safe to run any time.

If you want to be extra safe, add this to the top of your RunPod start script — SSH into production and ensure Redis is up before starting the tunnel:

```bash
ssh rune@gorm.predictioninstitute.com \
    "cd ~/workspace/projects/gorm.ai && docker compose up -d redis"
```

Put that before the `ssh -f -N` tunnel line.
