[2026-03-25T06:46:16Z] [USER] ok, but the relative path was what I had before. And the models weren't downloaded to there
[2026-03-25T06:46:23Z] [CLAUDE] Right — the issue is that `_apply_hf_env` uses `os.environ.setdefault`, which only sets the var if it's **not already set**. But `pydantic-settings` loads `.env` into the `Settings` object, not into `os.environ`. So if nothing else sets `HF_HUB_CACHE` in the actual environment, `setdefault` works fine.

The more likely problem: `huggingface_hub` was imported somewhere **before** `_apply_hf_env` ran. The library reads `HF_HUB_CACHE` at import time into a module constant. By the time `_load_model` calls `_apply_hf_env`, it's too late — `huggingface_hub` already cached the default `~/.cache/huggingface/hub`.

Use the absolute path to be safe:

```
HF_HUB_CACHE=/home/rune/workspace/projects/gorm.ai/models/huggingface
```

This way even if `huggingface_hub` reads it at import time, it gets the right path.
