**What happened:** The worker restarted ~40 min into your simulation, killing the task mid-execution. The DB never got updated with `ended_at`, so the frontend still shows it as running.

Want me to mark these stuck simulations as failed in the database? I can set `ended_at = now()` for all 5 orphaned simulations so the UI reflects reality and you can re-run the task.
[2026-03-26T06:18:05Z] [USER] Yes, set as failed. Why is this not happening automatically=
[2026-03-26T06:25:07Z] [CLAUDE] Looks good. Here's a summary of the two problems and the two fixes:

**Problem 1: Worker restarts with the same name → orphan detection skips its old tasks.**
The `mark_orphaned_worker_tasks_failed()` method only marks tasks from *dead* workers. When worker `GORM` restarts as `GORM`, its stuck tasks look like they belong to a live worker.

**Fix:** New `mark_worker_tasks_failed()` method called from `worker_ready` signal — on startup, the worker marks any `started` tasks under its own name as failed before accepting new work.

**Problem 2: Orphan detection only updates `task_records`, not `simulations.ended_at`.**
Even when tasks were correctly marked as failed, the `simulations` table was never updated, so `ended_at` stayed `NULL`.

**Fix:** New `_close_simulations_for_tasks()` helper called from all three failure-marking methods. It sets `ended_at = now()` on simulations linked to the failed tasks.

