- Now creates properly-shaped `np.empty((n, 0))` arrays and skips Ridge fitting entirely (sets `adj = np.zeros(horizon)`)
- Affected engines: timesfm, chronos2, kairos, flowstate, sundial, tirex, yinglong

With both fixes, re-running the same optimization should work — simulations will produce actual scores instead of crashing on the broadcast error, and even if some fail, the results will save correctly to the database.
