[2026-03-29T04:54:20Z] [CLAUDE] So `00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000011` is TimesFM. The 42 records use the UUID — they were written by the Celery service. The script on RunPod uses the slug `"timesfm"`, but its records aren't in this database at all.

The problem is that the RunPod script's `DATABASE_URL` is either not pointing to this database, or the script isn't writing progress records. The 42 records are old ones from a previous Celery-based run.

This is a configuration issue on RunPod, not a code issue. The RunPod script needs `DATABASE_URL` set to the GORM server's PostgreSQL (with the `+asyncpg` prefix) to write progress records back.

But regardless — even if the script had the right DB connection, it would write `engine="timesfm"` (slug) while the count query was looking for the UUID. The fix I just made handles that by checking both. Once you verify that RunPod's `DATABASE_URL` points to the GORM server's database, the counts will work.

