[2026-03-30T15:14:01Z] [CLAUDE] All pre-existing issues, none from my changes. The changes add:

1. **`socket_keepalive=True`** on both the broker transport and the Redis client — keeps TCP connections alive so they don't get dropped by intermediate firewalls/NAT during long idle periods (like during a 10+ minute rsync)
2. **`retry_on_timeout=True`** — Redis client automatically retries on timeout instead of immediately raising
3. **`socket_connect_timeout=5`** — fail fast on connect rather than hanging
4. **`broker_connection_retry_on_startup=True`** — Celery retries broker connection on worker startup if Redis isn't immediately reachable

These won't fix the immediate issue (the connection was already lost), but will make the remote workers much more resilient to transient network issues going forward.
