[2026-03-31T01:59:36Z] [CLAUDE] The fix: the `prevCidRef` was initialized with `cid` (which is `""` on first render), and the restore effect required `prevCidRef.current` to be truthy — so it never ran on initial mount. Now it initializes to `""` explicitly and fires whenever `cid` changes to any different value, including the first time the real customer ID arrives. This ensures `selectedGroupId` loads from localStorage for the right customer, and when there's no saved value, `effectiveGroupId` correctly falls through to `production_group_id` from customer_configuration.
[2026-03-31T02:07:38Z] [USER] My outlet group and other selection are still reset when I refresh screen
[2026-03-31T02:08:16Z] [CLAUDE] The problem was a race condition: when `cid` changed from `""` to the real customer ID, React batched the state updates from the restore effect together with the persist effects that also re-ran due to `cid` changing. The persist effects would fire with the old default values and overwrite the saved data before the restored values took effect.

The fix uses a `readyToSaveRef` gate: when the customer ID changes, persistence is disabled, the saved values are restored, and persistence is re-enabled via `requestAnimationFrame` after the state has settled. This ensures the restore completes before any persist effects can write.
