[2026-03-31T04:41:11Z] [CLAUDE] The fix: added `--build-arg BACKEND_INTERNAL_URL=http://app:8000` to the frontend build.

**What was happening:** The frontend image was built without `BACKEND_INTERNAL_URL`, so the Next.js rewrite that proxies client-side `/backend/*` requests was baked in pointing to `http://localhost:8000`. Inside the Docker network, `localhost` is the frontend container itself — not the FastAPI service. Login worked because Better Auth uses Prisma which connects directly to the DB at runtime, bypassing the rewrite entirely.

To fix the deployed site, rebuild and restart the frontend:

```bash
docker build --network=host -f frontend/Dockerfile --target runner \
  --build-arg NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://gorm.predictioninstitute.com \
  --build-arg BETTER_AUTH_URL=https://gorm.predictioninstitute.com \
  --build-arg BACKEND_INTERNAL_URL=http://app:8000 \
  -t gormai-frontend-prod frontend/

docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.prod.yml up -d frontend-prod
```

Or just re-run `bash scripts/deploy.sh`.
