The migration is already complete on your side, so the deadlock would have resolved once one process was killed (PostgreSQL auto-kills one). The prediction task on vast.ai likely got the error and failed.

You should be able to simply re-run the prediction task. The deadlock was a one-time collision, not a recurring issue - it only happened because we ran a migration while a task was actively writing to the database.

If it happens again in the future, the fix is to avoid running `alembic upgrade head` while heavy tasks are in progress. You could add a check in the migration workflow to verify no active Celery tasks before migrating.
