[2026-04-01T05:38:26Z] [CLAUDE] For your workload (TimesFM, Moirai2, Chronos2 - all PyTorch-based transformer models), use **`vastai/pytorch`**.

**Why:**
- All your prediction engines depend on PyTorch + CUDA
- TimesFM fine-tuning needs PyTorch with GPU support and proper CUDA drivers
- `vastai/pytorch` comes with PyTorch, CUDA, cuDNN pre-installed and tested against vast.ai's GPU drivers
- `vastai/base-image` is just Ubuntu + CUDA runtime - you'd have to install PyTorch yourself and risk version mismatches with the host GPU driver

**Which tag:** Pick one matching your PyTorch version. Your `pyproject.toml` has `torch>=2.0.0`. Use the latest 2.x tag, e.g. `vastai/pytorch:2.5.1-py3.11-cuda12.4` (match your Python 3.11).

**What you'd add on top:** Your `uv sync` to install the project dependencies, since vast.ai mounts or clones your code into the container.
