[2026-04-01T12:02:24Z] [CLAUDE] This was a pre-existing bug that only surfaced now because the query is `enabled: !!userId` — on first render `userId` is undefined, so `customers` is empty and `activeCustomer` is null, triggering the early return before the hooks. On the next render (once the session loads), all hooks run, causing the mismatch.

Moved all hooks (`useRef`, `useState`, `useEffect`, `useCallback`) above the early returns so they always execute in the same order.
