<li class="my-0.5"><strong class="font-semibold">Range:</strong> ~7,252 unit variance across the half-year</li>
</ul>
<p class="my-1">⚠️ <strong class="font-semibold">Note:</strong> The zone_id data appears to have limited granularity with all outlets mapped to a single zone. If you have multiple zones defined elsewhere (e.g., in <code class="rounded bg-[rgba(128,128,128,0.15)] px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.85em]">outlet_type</code>, <code class="rounded bg-[rgba(128,128,128,0.15)] px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.85em]">city</code>, or <code class="rounded bg-[rgba(128,128,128,0.15)] px-1 py-0.5 text-[0.85em]">state</code>), I can create a more detailed heatmap. Would you like me to create a heatmap using a different dimension like:</p>
<ul class="my-1 pl-5 list-disc">
