[2026-04-02T03:57:45Z] [CLAUDE] Done. Tables now render with:
- Rounded border container with horizontal scroll for wide tables
- Header row with muted background
- Divider lines between rows
- Hover highlight on rows
- Proper padding and alignment
- Compact text size (`text-xs`) to fit more columns
[2026-04-02T03:59:04Z] [USER] Add a copy button to the chat boxes. Should be similar to for instance the copy button on the ID input element, under tab details on page: predictions/strategies
[2026-04-02T04:02:02Z] [CLAUDE] Done. Each message bubble now has a copy button that:
- Appears on hover below the message text
- Uses the same animated `CopyIcon` from the strategies page
- Shows a green checkmark for 2 seconds after copying
- Shows a "Copied to clipboard" toast
- Works on both user and assistant messages
- Has a clipboard fallback for non-HTTPS environments
[2026-04-02T07:06:48Z] [USER] ultrathink. [1:44 PM] Magnus Gabrielsen
I want you to critically evaluate a product idea and challenge all assumptions. Do not be optimistic by default — I want a realistic and skeptical assessment.


⸻
CONTEXT


We are considering building a SaaS product for IT service providers (MSPs) and IT consultants.


The product is a “Vendor Risk Monitoring” platform.


The core idea:


    •    Monitor third-party vendors used by customers


    •    Detect risks such as:


    •    SSL certificate expiration


    •    DNS / MX issues


    •    Downtime / instability


    •    Known vulnerabilities (CVEs)


    •    Data breaches or incidents


    •    Translate technical signals into:


    •    Customer impact


    •    Risk level


    •    Recommended actions


The product would present:


    •    A dashboard of customers


    •    Which vendors are causing risk


    •    What actions to take


The goal is to make IT providers more proactive and efficient.


⸻
CORE QUESTION


Is this a viable and realistic product — or are we underestimating key challenges?


⸻
