[2026-04-04T03:29:05Z] [CLAUDE] This error means the installed PyTorch was compiled for a different CUDA compute capability than your GPU has. It's not related to the multi-GPU changes.

What GPU do you have, and how is PyTorch installed? Run:

```bash
python -c "import torch; print(torch.__version__); print(torch.version.cuda); print(torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)); print(torch.cuda.get_device_capability(0))"
```

The most common cause: PyTorch's default pip/uv install ships with CUDA 12.x kernels that support compute capability 5.0+, but some older or unusual GPUs aren't covered. Alternatively, if you installed a CPU-only build of PyTorch, it won't have any CUDA kernels at all.
