[2026-04-04T05:12:00Z] [CLAUDE] Yes, that's normal. `flash-attn` compiles CUDA kernels from source for your specific GPU architecture — on a single machine it typically takes 10-30 minutes depending on CPU cores and whether it's compiling for multiple CUDA architectures.

You can speed it up by setting the `MAX_JOBS` env var (defaults to all cores, but compilation is memory-hungry) and restricting to only your GPU arch. But for now just let it finish — it only needs to compile once.
