[2026-04-04T10:20:10Z] [CLAUDE] That's the bug. The `insights_worker` was being loaded from the customer config (line 870) but never passed to the `PredictionRequest`. Without the `worker` field, the task gets picked up by any available Celery worker — likely one that doesn't have `tirex-ts` installed. Since `allow_fallback` is disabled for this customer, the prediction fails instead of falling back to statistical.

The fix adds `worker=worker` to the request so the task gets routed to the correct worker (the one configured with TiRex support).
