[2026-04-05T02:42:01Z] [USER] What possible parameters does Chronos Bolt take?
[2026-04-05T02:42:26Z] [CLAUDE] Chronos-Bolt inherits from `Chronos2DirectEngine`, so it takes the same 4 parameters (defined in `apply_parameters` at line 104):

| Parameter | Description | Default (Bolt) |
|-----------|-------------|----------------|
| `model` / `submodel` | HuggingFace model ID or short name | `amazon/chronos-bolt-base` |
| `samples` | Monte-Carlo sample paths (ignored for Bolt — it outputs quantiles directly) | N/A |
| `precision` | Torch dtype: `float32`, `bfloat16`, `float16` | `bfloat16` |
| `batch_size` | Outlets per forward pass | `8` |

Available Bolt model sizes: `chronos-bolt-tiny`, `chronos-bolt-mini`, `chronos-bolt-small`, `chronos-bolt-base`.

Note that `samples` has no effect on Bolt since it produces quantiles natively in a single forward pass instead of drawing sample paths.
