[2026-04-05T12:00:33Z] [CLAUDE] Here's a summary of the changes:

**Root cause**: `pynvml` was never a project dependency, so the primary GPU detection method always failed silently on workers. The torch fallback also silently swallowed exceptions. If both failed (e.g., CUDA init issues at startup), no GPU info was stored in Redis and the dashboard showed "No GPU".

**Changes made**:

1. **`pyproject.toml`** — Added `nvidia-ml-py3>=7.352.0` as a core dependency so `pynvml` is available on all workers.

2. **`resource_estimator.py`** — Added an `nvidia-smi` CLI fallback as a third detection method (after pynvml and torch). Also added `logger.debug()` calls to all exception handlers so GPU detection failures are no longer invisible.

3. **`celery_app.py`** — Added `logging` import and logger. Added `logger.info()`/`logger.warning()`/`logger.exception()` to both `on_worker_ready` and `_refresh_worker_registry` GPU sections. If GPU detection fails, the logs will now show exactly why.

After deploying, the Vast Moirai worker should detect the RTX 5070 Ti via pynvml (preferred) or nvidia-smi (fallback). If it still doesn't work, the logs will now tell you exactly which detection method failed and why.
