[2026-04-05T12:01:14Z] [USER] Does the vast server need to be restarted?
[2026-04-05T12:01:21Z] [CLAUDE] Yes — the GPU detection runs during the Celery `worker_ready` signal (at startup) and lazily on the first task via `_refresh_worker_registry`. Since `pynvml` wasn't installed before, both paths would have failed silently.

After deploying the updated dependencies, restarting the Vast worker will trigger `on_worker_ready` which will now successfully detect the RTX 5070 Ti via `pynvml` and store it in Redis.

Alternatively, if you don't want to restart, the lazy path in `_refresh_worker_registry` will try again on the next task — but only if `nvidia-ml-py3` gets installed first (e.g., via `uv sync` on the worker).
