A note on what to expect:
- On a 32 GB box: `MAX_JOBS=8` (was 12+) — should fit, build takes ~30 min
- On a 16 GB box: `MAX_JOBS=4` — slower (~60 min) but won't OOM
- On a 64 GB box: `MAX_JOBS=16` capped to nproc

If you keep hitting OOM even after this, the next lever is hardcoding `MAX_JOBS=2` — flash-attn from source on torch nightly is genuinely a memory hog and 2 jobs is the safe-everywhere setting.

Longer-term, the cleanest escape from this whole mess is to switch to a vast.ai image that has flash-attn pre-installed (the `pytorch/pytorch` images don't, but several Hugging Face / NVIDIA NGC images do), so `uv sync` can skip the source build entirely.
