[2026-04-08T02:26:12Z] [CLAUDE] Yes — Claude Code persists conversations automatically. A few options:

**Resume a previous session:**
- `claude --continue` (or `claude -c`) — resumes your most recent conversation in the current directory
- `claude --resume` (or `claude -r`) — opens a picker to choose from past conversations in this directory

**From inside a session:**
- `/resume` — pick a past conversation to jump back into

Sessions are stored per working directory under `~/.claude/projects/<dir-slug>/`, so running `claude -c` from `/home/rune/workspace/projects/gorm.ai` will pick up where you left off here.

If you want to preserve specific facts across sessions (not just resume one), tell me to remember them and I'll write them to the auto-memory system — those are loaded into every future conversation in this project regardless of which session you resume.
