The massive difference is in **d_g2 (lost sales)**: the standalone "All off" simulation has d_g2 = **-$3,050** vs the exploration's WPC OFF at **-$542**. The standalone also has much worse d_g3 (-$1,271 vs -$476).

**The problem isn't the code — it's that the standalone simulations aren't an apples-to-apples WPC comparison.** Your standalone simulation named "All off" likely has other settings turned off too (variation adjustment, possibly others), and "VA" has them turned on. So the standalone comparison measures the combined effect of multiple settings, not just WPC.

The exploration correctly isolates WPC by only overriding `weekday_profile_correction` while keeping all other settings at their current customer defaults. It's the more trustworthy comparison for evaluating WPC alone.
