See attached image.

During the verification phase, we need to do a large number of checks, track errors & rows filtered out by "Allowed Values" & "Disallowed Values" .The results should be displayed in a table.

1) Ignore possible header
2) Verify that the number of elements in the input file match the number of elements on the inport template
3) If element in input template has defined "Allowed Values" (comma separated list) verify that the element in the input file is in this list.
4) If element in input template has defined "Disallowed Values" (comma separated list) verify that the element in the input file is NOT in this list.

5) "Can be Empty" => If false, verify that the element in the input file is not empty.
6) "Type" => if "Number", verify element is a number.

7) Element "Account ID" => verify element in the input file is not empty + not > 32 length
Element "Date" => verify element in the input file follow the Date Format (default to MM/DD/YYYY) and is well-formed (i.e., MM is a whole number between 1 & 12; DD is a whole number between 1 & 31, etc.)
Element "Start Date" => verify element in the input file follow the Date Format (default to MM/DD/YYYY) 
Element "End Date" => verify element in the input file follow the Date Format (default to MM/DD/YYYY) 
Element "Quantity" => verify element in the input file is a whole number larger than 0 + do not exceed "Maximum Value" (if set/!= 0) 
Element "Quantity Adjustment" => verify element in the input file is a whole number + do not exceed "Maximum Value" (if set/!= 0)
Element "Sold Net" => verify element in the input file is a whole number larger than 0 + do not exceed "Maximum Value" (if set/!= 0)
Element "Sold Scan" => verify element in the input file is a whole number larger than 0 + do not exceed "Maximum Value" (if set/!= 0)
Element "Return" => verify element in the input file is a whole number + do not exceed "Maximum Value" (if set/!= 0)

Element "Cost" => verify element in the input file is a number (float)
Element "Profit" => verify element in the input file is a number (float)
Element "Revenue" => verify element in the input file is a number (float)
Element "Day of Week" => verify element in the input file is either a number 1-7 or a text "Monday" .. "Sunday" or "Mon" .. "Sun"
Element "Fixed Quantity" => verify element in the input file is a whole number
Element "Monday Fixed Quantity" - "Sunday Fixed Quantity" => verify element in the input file is a whole number
Element "Minimum Quantity" => verify element in the input file is a whole number
Element "Monday Minimum Quantity" - "Sunday Minimum Quantity" => verify element in the input file is a whole number
Element "Maximum Quantity" => verify element in the input file is a whole number
Element "Open" => verify element in the input file is either 1/0, true/false, yes/no
Element "Monday Open" - "Sunday Open" => verify element in the input file is either 1/0, true/false, yes/no

8) "Allow Positive" => if False, make sure element in the input file is a positive number
9) "Allow Negative" => if False, make sure element in the input file is a negative number

