## What changed

`src/gorm_ai/tasks/simulations.py` — added a 60-second heartbeat that re-emits the latest progress while the simulation runs. Behavior:

- `_on_progress` now stashes the latest `(progress, message)` and persists immediately (unchanged behavior for explicit progress events).
- `_heartbeat` runs in the background, re-persisting the same values every 60s. This refreshes `updated_at` and `refresh_worker_registry()` (Redis heartbeat) — both signals the orphan detector relies on. No progress regression because percent/message stays the same.
- Wrapped the simulation call in try/finally so the heartbeat is always cancelled cleanly on success, exception, or graceful stop.
- Heartbeat exceptions are swallowed so a transient DB blip can't crash the simulation.

With `stale_seconds=600` on the orphan detector and a 60s heartbeat, you have 10× headroom — even if a few heartbeats miss the DB, the threshold won't trip.

