1. Run the recovery UPDATE (`task_id='8ac52c6b-…'` → status='started') so the running task shows up in the UI again. The vast worker will keep grinding and write `success` when it finishes.
2. Deploy the new `simulations.py` to the vast worker — but **only after** the current simulation finishes, since restarting the worker now would lose the in-flight chunks 13+.

