[2026-05-14T04:40:39Z] [CLAUDE] **SOTA = State Of The Art.** In ML it means "the current best-performing model on a benchmark" — e.g., when Google ships TimesFM 2.5 and it beats every prior model on standard time-series benchmarks, that's the new SOTA.

In the draft I used it in "As new SOTA models ship, we add them." For an investor audience that's probably too much jargon — better as "As new frontier models ship" or just "As new models ship."

Want me to do a jargon pass on the whole draft? There are a few more candidates (MAPE, foundation model, ensemble, quantile, Newsvendor) that might be worth either defining inline or swapping for plainer language depending on how technical your target investors are.
