The big cohort-wide events look like "the driver had a really bad Saturday" — but the *which-outlets-skipped* changes every time. TCS sees that as "no concentration" because no specific subset of outlets keeps appearing together. And the solo skips give TCS zero signal — concentration requires co-occurrence.

So the route fails TCS for two opposite reasons simultaneously: half the events are too sparse (solo) and the other half are too broad (everyone).

